  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Equation of auxiliary circle is\n$$\nx^2+y^2=9\n$$\nEquation of $A M$ is $\\frac{x}{3}+\\frac{y}{1}=1$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/Hod-rW6Zn2B0oS-2r5NrPWUUUlN7neIAYNLN1KktmLY.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\nOn solving Eqs. (i) and (ii), we get Coordinates of $M=\\left(-\\frac{12}{5}, \\frac{9}{5}\\right)$ Now, area of $\\triangle A O M=\\frac{1}{2} \\times O A \\times M N$ $=\\frac{27}{10}$ sq units",
    "image": null
  },
